# Template Architecture

## Core Rule

Templates are **presentation only**. They render UI from `WeddingData`; they never fetch DB, auth, payments, or business logic.

```tsx
<TemplateRenderer template="royal" data={weddingData} />
```

## Folder Structure

```
src/templates/
  TemplateRenderer.tsx
  shared/
    motion/
    sections/
    theme/
  /<template-id>/
    <Name>Template.tsx
    components/
    hooks/
    sections/
    theme.ts
    config/
```

Example: `src/templates/royal/RoyalTemplate.tsx` + `sections/HeroSection.tsx`, etc.

## Shared Data

All templates consume **`WeddingData`** from `src/types/`. Same schema for editor, preview, DB `content` JSONB, and publish.

## Reusability (Pragmatic)

- **100% shared:** hooks (`useWeddingCountdown`), UI atoms (buttons, typography wrappers)
- **Bespoke per template:** section components inside `src/templates/<id>/sections/` — template-specific Tailwind/colors OK for cinematic identity
- Do not force identical section UI across all templates (anti-pattern for premium feel)

## Section Flow (Storytelling)

Optional intro → Hero → Couple reveal → Countdown → Blessing → Events → Story → Gallery → RSVP → Venue → Thank You. Pace emotionally; avoid content dumps.

## Events

Support Indian events (Mehendi, Haldi, Wedding, Reception, Sangeet). Event shape: title, icon, description, date, time, venue, `googleMapLink`.

## Theme (Phase 2)

`ThemeConfig` is injected through `TemplateThemeProvider` as CSS variables. Each template owns default `TemplateThemeTokens` in `<template-id>/theme.ts`; `WeddingData.theme` is an override layer. Prefer `var(--template-primary)`, `var(--template-text)`, and related runtime variables over scattering literal colors.

## Section Contracts

Shared contracts live in `src/templates/shared/sections/types.ts`. New templates can keep bespoke section UI, but they should consume the same props so editor and publish logic remain stable.

## Animations

Framer Motion; modular; viewport reveals; subtle parallax-lite only. No GSAP-heavy or scroll-jacking.

## Performance

`next/image` + `sizes`; lazy gallery/maps; no unoptimized video heroes.

## Editor Compatibility

Editable fields map to future dashboard controls — don't couple copy into layout logic.

## Mobile

Mobile rendering and touch are primary; desktop secondary.

## Priority

1. emotional storytelling 2. mobile 3. smooth motion 4. scalable structure 5. performance
